    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5182" root="جد" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُجِدٌّ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَادٌّ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنَّهَا لمجدّة بِالرَّجُلِ</span>, a phrase
mentioned by As, said of a she-camel, meaning,
<i>Verily she is quick in her pace with the man:</i>
but Az says, I know not whether he said ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِجَدَّةٌ</span></b> 
or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُجِدَّةٌ</span>: the former would be from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَدَّ</span>; and
the latter, from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَجَدَّ</span>. (L.)

